    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0701" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/3875a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting American Representative to the French Committee of National
                        Liberation at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chapin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-20T00:00:00-04:00">May 20,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1574. For Murphy. We have been particularly interested in the telegrams which you
                    and Chapin have been sending on subject of de Gaulle’s denunciation of
                    Clark–Darlan Agreement and Assembly’s resolution that Committee adopt name of
                    provisional government of France.</p>
                <p>You are correct in your assumption that the question of revision of Clark–Darlan
                    agreement should be kept on military level and that if new agreement is achieved
                    it should be signed by Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
